# Update all docs when we discuss

When the user locks or changes product, architecture, APIs, or tests in chat, **edit the docs in the same turn**. Do not leave the answer only in conversation.

Touch every folder that the change hits:

- `docs/prd/<module>.md` — behaviour, stories, policies
- `docs/trd/<module>.md` — contracts, schema, config
- `docs/decision/` — only if it is an architecture choice (new file or edit)
- `docs/testing/` — unit / integration / e2e if behaviour is testable
- `docs/architecture.md` — if the runtime flow changed
- `docs/adr/` — if a hard-to-reverse trade-off changed
- `CONTEXT.md` — if a glossary term changed
- `AGENTS.md` — if a standing constraint changed

Do not write application code (`pom.xml`, `src/`, Dockerfiles) while discussing. Docs only until the user explicitly asks to implement.
